WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.490
Let's take a moment to review slip. Using

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:10.540
the slip setting of your machine, needles
in B or working position will not knit.

3
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:16.140
This is used for the slip stitch technique
and knitting in the round with the ribber.

4
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.580
It's also referred to as free pass.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.540
Let's say you need to move your carriage

6
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.020
from one side of the bed to the other
without knitting or dropping

7
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.460
stitches. Keep all needles in B.

8
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:34.660
Set your carriage to slip and you can
safely pass it across the knitting.

9
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:41.940
On some knitting machines, you can set
the cam to slip, left, right or both.

10
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:47.340
With the Taitexma 160, there is
only one part lever. Engaging

11
00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.580
that part lever means needles in working

12
00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.700
or B position will slip
in both directions.

13
00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:57.520
To knit I-cord or anytime you want

14
00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:03.640
to alternate slipping and knitting
you need to move the lever.

15
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:15.800
With the part lever engaged, I'm pushing
my carriage right and the needles slip.

16
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:22.920
You can see that the stitches didn't knit
and the yarn is just carried across.

17
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.660
Move the lever to plain and it will

18
00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:30.930
cancel the slip and knit
the stitches when I knit back.

19
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:37.260
We create I-cord by alternating slip and
knit with the passing of the carriage.

20
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.660
This can get really tedious on this

21
00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.820
machine if you're flipping
that lever back and forth.

22
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:46.620
But there is an easier way.

23
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:47.700
One more time.

24
00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.540
With the part lever engaged,
needles in B will slip.

25
00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:55.840
But needles in D or E will knit.

26
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.120
So to knit I-cord,
put three or four needles into working or

27
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:09.780
B position, pass the carriage
left and the needles will slip.

28
00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:15.520
Pull out the needles to D or E position,
pass the carriage and then stitches will

29
00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:19.940
knit and they're all
returned to B position.

30
00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:25.700
With the needles in B pass
that carriage left and the needles slip.

31
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:28.600
Pull the needles out and the stitches will

32
00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:33.640
knit and they'll automatically
be put back into B position.

33
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.890
This is so much easier.

34
00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.450
No need to flip that part lever

35
00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.160
back and forth.

36
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.260
Here's an example of free pass.

37
00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:57.820
My carriage is set to slip,
the cam lever is set to part.

38
00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:03.610
When I pull out needles, they will
knit even though part is engaged.

39
00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.300
With the needles remaining in B position,

40
00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.960
I can free pass back and the
stitches won't knit or drop.

